{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The  point  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  is  a  point  on  a  circle  with  center  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Perpendicular  lines  are  drawn  from  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  to perpendicular  diameters,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />  and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />,  meeting  them  at  points  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />  and  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />,  respectively.  If  the  diameter  of  the  circle  is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,  what  is  the  length  of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9400b5f4774c678b337f6ad85b4cd4de3a1dff86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\,4\\quad\\mathrm{(B)}\\,8\\quad\\mathrm{(C)}\\,6\\sqrt{3}\\quad\\mathrm{(D)}\\,4\\sqrt{3}\\quad\\mathrm{(E)}\\,4\\sqrt{2}\\quad\\mathrm{(F)}\\,12\\quad\\mathrm{(G)}\\,6\\quad\\mathrm{(H)}\\,\\text{none of the above}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"633\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4db8010315ec6af737ec160163afe29f84d98b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair P=(-60,80), A=(-100,0), B=(100,0), C=(0,100), D=(0,-100), Y=(-60,0), Z=(0,80); draw(circle((0,0),100)); draw(A--B); draw(C--D); draw(Y--P--Z); draw(Y--Z); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,0),SE); dot(P); label(&quot;P&quot;,P,NW); dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,W); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,E); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,N); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,S); dot(Y); label(&quot;Y&quot;,Y,S); dot(Z); label(&quot;Z&quot;,Z,E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65fe8f0116701b8eb24fa0c5fb7ed80274530976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\perp CD, AB \\perp PY, CD \\perp PZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"258\" height=\"16\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f21351a0c661db0e870439f3d2598bfbcfdf675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PYOZ$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a>.  The diagonal of a rectangle is the same length, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/8/e9807ae2f53eb2db8b67164990cb5e7ba379e192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ = PO$\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25fe9bf59f0b24dfa18ae578c071f8fffaf7c7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> is the radius of the circle, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4f3fdc688a1cf9a51f84f67f9a732ea4e9bedfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 \\cdot 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\,8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href